From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "fpgas.online build" <builds@fpgas.online>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:53:08 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 36/37] board: fomu_evt_header, the Fomu EVT's iCE40 SRAM load
 over a Pi header

SPI_GPIO_BOARD describes an FPGA whose SPI port is wired to host GPIO
lines: GPIO numbers rather than FTDI masks, GPIO_NC for an unwired pin,
cable libgpiod. fomu_evt_header is the Fomu EVT on a Raspberry Pi header
(BCM numbers): CRESET_B 27, CDONE 17, SPI_SS 8, SPI_SCK 11, SPI_SI 9 (the
Pi's MISO pin: the Pi's SPI0 cannot drive it), SPI_SO 10, flash /HOLD 25.

With the libgpiod cable, SPI mode goes to gpio_spi_comm(): an iCE40
board is required, the load is SRAM only and the default (-f, --verify,
--detect, --reset and the flash options are refused), and --pins is
MOSI:MISO:SCK:CS[:HOLDN], MOSI being the host's output into SPI_SI. A
GPIO-wired board with any other cable is refused, so its GPIO numbers
are never used as FTDI pin masks. Failures exit non-zero.

    openFPGALoader -b fomu_evt_header design.bin

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JG8Wtod8kFmcquwN34pFCa
